                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Let me start this off by saying: I love and have loved this game since childhood.\nI am dumb and I do not get how to do 99% of the things on this game. But that never stopped me as a child (past not knowing I had to pause the game when I closed it and all my villagers died...) of playing it.\n\nHowever, this game is not optimized on steam. As other people have stated, it's an old game and clearly made for old computers. You cannot resize it, it glitches if you tab out of the game, and just overall not made for the newer monitors/multiple screens.\nThat wouldn't be an issue, I recognize this is a very old game! This wouldn't bother me as bad if I didn't know about the other issue.\n\nIt's FREE on their website. While steam is convenient, it's a lot more convenient to just hit download on their actual website.\nNot to mention a lot of the issues for monitors are fixed on the FREE version.\n\nI absolutely adore this game and I do actually recommend people play it, especially if they've played it in their childhood. It doesn't compare to new age games obviously, but it's still fun to play and mess around with.\nI don't recommend buying it here though.",
